The dictionaries of lexspell (nylex's spelling program)
=======================================================

They are made by tools/mkdict.py from Hunspell dictionaries, as
LibreOffice has them (github.com/LibreOffice/dictionaries, commit
67032ee9, October 2026):

  sv.dict     Swedish, from sv_SE.aff and sv_SE.dic: "Den stora svenska
              ordlistan", Copyright (C) 2003-19 Goran Andersson
              <goran@init.se>, under the GNU Lesser General Public
              License version 3 (COPYING.LGPL-3, with COPYING.GPL-3,
              which it refers to; README_sv_SE.txt).
  en_GB.dict  British English, from en_GB.aff and en_GB.dic (Marco A.G.
              Pinto and others, based on Kevin Atkinson's SCOWL), under
              the LGPL as well (README_en_GB.txt).
  en_US.dict  American English, from en_US.aff and en_US.dic (Kevin
              Atkinson's SCOWL), under SCOWL's permissive licence and
              Ispell's BSD licence (README_en_US.txt).

The .aff and .dic files here are the sources of the .dict files, as
they were; "make dicts" (python3) makes the .dict files again.  The
word lists are data that lexspell reads; lexspell itself is nylex's.

    python3 tools/mkdict.py dict/sv_SE.aff dict/sv_SE.dic sv.dict sv

On the D-NIX Amiga port the README_xx_XX.txt files are README.xx_XX
(its file names are at most 14 characters).
